# RxDB schema changes

Changing an existing collection schema **without incrementing `version`** causes `DB6`: "another instance created this collection with a different schema".

This includes any hash-changing edit: properties, `required`, `indexes`, `multipleOf`, types, defaults.

## Checklist (every schema edit)

1. Increment `version` in `src/services/rxdb/schemas/<collection>Schema.ts`. Do **not** edit an already-shipped version in place.
2. Add `migrationStrategies[newVersion]` in `src/services/rxdb/database.ts` for that collection. Keep every previous strategy.
3. If you only changed constraints (e.g. `required`, `multipleOf`) and documents already match, use an identity migration: `(oldDoc) => oldDoc`.
4. If you added a field, set it on every old doc in the migration (never leave required fields missing).
5. If this version was already loaded in a local DB, bump **again**. Same version + different hash = `DB6`.

```ts
// Schema: version: 2
// database.ts
teams: {
  schema: teamSchema,
  migrationStrategies: {
    1: withCreatedAt,
    2: (oldDoc) => oldDoc, // or transform
  },
},
```

Never reuse a version number after anyone may have opened the app with it.
